      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "This applies to all generic controllers including non-xinput gamepads like PS4/PS3/Dualshock controllers. Like you said it's a common Unity problem, caused by their extremely outdated input manager which is only just now being addressed in Unity 2019 - https://blogs.unity3d.com/2019/10/14/introducing-the-new-input-system/\n\nIdeally until the new system can be used, VRC could switch to a more robust solution like Rewired - https://assetstore.unity.com/packages/tools/utilities/rewired-21676",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
