  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2018-02-21T06:16:48.189Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "This is a common problem with Unity that really should be fixed by default.\n\nUnity takes input from every joystick like USB device and interprets it as a gamepad. This means users in VR who have other controllers have to unplug everything before playing in order to prevent false inputs.\n\nFor me, my menus constantly scroll up, so I can't select anything in the UI that isn't at the top. You can hear a UI sound effect spamming constantly for as long as the menu is open.\n\nIn my case, I have:\nThrustmaster HOTAS\nUSB MFCDs\nSaitek Combat Flight Pedals\n\nNone of these are gamepads. Please disable gamepad input when motion controls are detected. There is no reasonable use case for using a gamepad and motion controllers at the same time.",
